# (each content-verified via secondary fetch 2026-08-19).
https://business.adobe.com/.*
https://quickbooks.intuit.com/.*
https://www.servicenow.com/.*
https://www.turkishairlines.com/.*
https://www.uber.com/.*
# Radware Bot Manager (returns nonstandard 247 to non-browsers); site alive.
https://www.alice.co.il/.*
# TLS refused to curl/lychee, content verified via a second fetch channel 2026-09-06 (docs.inlace.co also 200); site alive.
https://inlace.co/.*
# unsplash.com — lychee got 401 from the GitHub runner on 2026-09-15 (issue #17); a direct fetch the same day
# returned 200 with real content. Bot-armored against the checker's TLS fingerprint, not dead.
https://unsplash.com/.*
# getyourguide.com — lychee failed with "HTTP/2 protocol error" from the runner on 2026-09-15 (issue #17).
# A direct fetch the same day returned 403, which this workflow already accepts; the break is the HTTP/2
# negotiation, not the status. Site alive.
https://www.getyourguide.com/.*
# www.adobe.com — resets curl/lychee on both HTTP/1.1 and HTTP/2 (INTERNAL_ERROR) from a residential network on
# 2026-09-25; a second fetch channel (Exa crawl) the same day returned the real homepage. Same class as business.adobe.com.
https://www.adobe.com/.*
